  "section_notes": "S2 sets a 5% corrective-action trigger with no sales-stop, so a model like Hearth 10 at 6.2% can keep selling while it remediates, and per-model rates go to customers and regulators but not the public. S5 makes a mandatory recall at 8 per 100,000 per rolling 12 months with no transition, which captures Ember 8 at 9.9 but not Hearth 10 at 6.4. S3's 72-month retrofit deadline with a feasibility escape and S4's 36-month built-in suppression start both sit inside the acceptable ranges."
